b*(n) = smallest absolute burst reaching stakes-weighted 90%:
   n      b*     b*/n   b*/sqrt(n)
  10       5     0.50         1.58
  20       5     0.25         1.12
  40      20     0.50         3.16
  80      20     0.25         2.24

  Read: whichever of b*/n or b*/sqrt(n) is ~flat across n is the scaling.
  Flat b* (both columns falling) => burst is ~constant in n.
